A pattern with a literal of two or more bytes between stars matches a
value that has it after an unknown part. The string solver found the
literal's index_of to be -1: each counter-example instance of its
not-contains constraint was at one position chosen by the witness
function, which the next model moved, until it gave up and took the model
as a counterexample.
